+   // pack: main thread caught mid-lookup during a live TPS dip). GameRules.getBoolean()
+   // does a Guava ImmutableMap hash lookup on every single call even though the
+   // underlying BooleanValue object's IDENTITY never changes for a given (Level, Key)
+   // pair — only its internal boolean mutates in place via /gamerule. Caching the VALUE
+   // OBJECT reference (not the boolean) keeps this correctly live across gamerule
+   // changes while skipping the repeated map lookup. Guava MapMaker with weakKeys()
+   // instead of a plain ConcurrentHashMap: WaterFluid.Source/Flowing are process-wide
+   // singletons shared across region threads (needs thread-safety), but a strong-keyed
+   // map would pin every Level this ever sees alive forever — weak keys let entries for
+   // unloaded/discarded Level instances (test worlds, mod-managed dimensions) get
+   // collected instead of leaking.
+   private final java.util.Map<Level, GameRules.BooleanValue> nestworldWaterSourceConversionCache =
+         new com.google.common.collect.MapMaker().weakKeys().makeMap();
